<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Staffarda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1690</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war">Nine Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Staffarda was fought on 18 August 1690 near the abbey of Staffarda, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war">Nine Years' War</a>. A French army under Marshal Catinat defeated Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-amadeus-ii">Victor Amadeus II</a> of Savoy and his Spanish allies, after the duke had joined the Grand Alliance against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>. The defeat exposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> to French occupation and plunder, as did a second defeat at Marsaglia in 1693.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-staffarda.jpg" alt="Battle of Staffarda" width="320" height="175" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Bickham the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_battle_of_Staffard_in_Piedmont.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
